1
00:00:03,433 --> 00:00:05,266
I'm Peppa Pig. [snorts]

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:08,033
-This is my little brother, George.
-[snorts]

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,299
-This is Mommy Pig.
-[Mommy Pig snorts]

4
00:00:10,366 --> 00:00:12,066
And this is Daddy Pig.

5
00:00:12,133 --> 00:00:14,133
-[Daddy Pig snorts]
-[all laugh]

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,766
Peppa Pig. [snorts]

7
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,766
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,166
[narrator] It is a lovely sunny morning.

9
00:00:22,233 --> 00:00:23,799
[snorts] Ah.

10
00:00:24,033 --> 00:00:27,533
What a nice day for doing nothing.

11
00:00:27,599 --> 00:00:29,733
[narrator] Daddy Pig loves doing nothing.

12
00:00:29,799 --> 00:00:33,233
[snorts] Daddy, aren't you going
to work today?

13
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,766
No, Peppa, it's Saturday.

14
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,166
[narrator] Daddy Pig doesn't work
on Saturdays.

15
00:00:38,233 --> 00:00:40,733
[snorts] Daddy Pig,
you'll be late for work.

16
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:43,300
But it's Saturday, Mommy Pig.

17
00:00:43,366 --> 00:00:46,400
-Isn't it?
-No, it's Thursday.

18
00:00:46,466 --> 00:00:47,566
[Daddy Pig yells]

19
00:00:47,633 --> 00:00:50,000
[narrator] Daddy Pig works on Thursdays.

20
00:00:50,066 --> 00:00:51,000
See you later.

21
00:00:51,066 --> 00:00:52,300
[Peppa &amp; George] Bye-bye.

22
00:00:52,366 --> 00:00:55,466
[snorts] Poor Daddy, having to work.

23
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:59,166
Lucky Mommy,
you can play at home all day.

24
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:01,000
I'm not playing.

25
00:01:01,066 --> 00:01:03,233
I'm working on my computer.

26
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:04,233
[George snorts]

27
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:08,000
[narrator] George wants to play
the Happy Mrs. Chicken game.

28
00:01:08,566 --> 00:01:11,633
George, we can play
the Happy Mrs. Chicken game

29
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:13,366
after I've finished my work.

30
00:01:13,433 --> 00:01:14,800
-Oh.
-[horn honks]

31
00:01:15,399 --> 00:01:19,233
[narrator] Mommy Sheep and Suzy have come
to pick up Peppa for playgroup.

32
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,300
[bleats] Hello, Peppa.

33
00:01:21,366 --> 00:01:23,033
[snorts] Hello, Suzy.

34
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:24,100
[Peppa &amp; Suzy giggle]

35
00:01:24,166 --> 00:01:25,633
Have a good day at playgroup.

36
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:28,466
Bye-bye, Mommy. Work hard.

37
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:35,133
Mrs. Sheep, do you work or do you play?

38
00:01:35,199 --> 00:01:37,699
I'm going to be working very hard today.

39
00:01:37,766 --> 00:01:40,133
[bleats] I'm off to the gym.

40
00:01:40,199 --> 00:01:42,266
What do you do at the gym?

41
00:01:42,333 --> 00:01:45,100
Running, jumping and skipping.

42
00:01:45,166 --> 00:01:49,800
Mommy, that's not work. That's play.

43
00:01:50,033 --> 00:01:52,033
[all laughing]

44
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,800
[narrator] Peppa and Suzy have arrived
at the playgroup.

45
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:58,066
[Peppa &amp; Suzy] Hello, everyone.

46
00:01:58,133 --> 00:02:00,533
[students] Hello, Peppa. Hello, Suzy.

47
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:01,566
[students giggling]

48
00:02:01,633 --> 00:02:06,399
Ah-ho. Children, today we will play shops.

49
00:02:06,466 --> 00:02:07,733
[all] Ooh.

50
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,600
Who wants to be shopkeeper?

51
00:02:09,666 --> 00:02:11,200
[students] Me, me, me!

52
00:02:11,266 --> 00:02:13,633
Peppa and Suzy can be shopkeepers.

53
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:16,466
Everyone else can be customers.

54
00:02:16,533 --> 00:02:19,733
[narrator] Peppa and Suzy are going to run
a pretend shop.

55
00:02:19,799 --> 00:02:22,200
What do we have to do?

56
00:02:22,266 --> 00:02:27,133
I will take the money, Suzy,
and you can stack the shelves.

57
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,100
Okay.

58
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,166
[narrator] Danny Dog
is the first customer.

59
00:02:31,233 --> 00:02:33,000
Hello, shopkeeper.

60
00:02:33,066 --> 00:02:34,333
Hello, Mr. Dog.

61
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:37,166
Can I have some biscuits, please?

62
00:02:37,233 --> 00:02:40,000
Suzy, have we got any biscuits?

63
00:02:40,066 --> 00:02:43,233
No, but we've got a toy telephone.

64
00:02:43,299 --> 00:02:45,200
How much will that be?

65
00:02:45,266 --> 00:02:48,566
That will be a hundred pounds, please.

66
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,066
[giggles] Thank you.

67
00:02:52,133 --> 00:02:53,633
Next, please.

68
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:55,799
[neighs] Hello, shopkeeper.

69
00:02:56,433 --> 00:02:58,700
Can I have a loaf of bread, please?

70
00:02:58,766 --> 00:03:02,066
No, but you can have a toy house.

71
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:04,433
Would you like it in a bag, sir?

72
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,266
Yes, please.

73
00:03:06,333 --> 00:03:09,399
That will be one penny, please.

74
00:03:11,066 --> 00:03:13,600
Oh, I haven't got enough money.

75
00:03:13,666 --> 00:03:16,333
You can pay us next time you come in.

76
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:19,266
Gosh, this is hard work.

77
00:03:19,333 --> 00:03:20,399
Yes.

78
00:03:21,066 --> 00:03:22,799
[squeaks] Hello, shopkeeper.

79
00:03:23,033 --> 00:03:27,200
What can I buy
for a million thousand pounds, please?

80
00:03:27,266 --> 00:03:32,166
Suzy, what have we got
for a million thousand pounds?

81
00:03:32,233 --> 00:03:33,466
Hmm.

82
00:03:33,533 --> 00:03:35,033
A carrot?

83
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:36,266
Yes, please.

84
00:03:36,333 --> 00:03:38,299
[narrator] Rebecca Rabbit likes carrots.

85
00:03:38,366 --> 00:03:40,100
[all giggle]

86
00:03:40,166 --> 00:03:41,433
[ringing]

87
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:44,033
-[narrator] It is home time.
-[students giggling]

88
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:46,700
[narrator] Daddy Pig has come
to collect Peppa and Suzy.

89
00:03:47,666 --> 00:03:48,566
[horn honks]

90
00:03:48,633 --> 00:03:51,399
Daddy, have you had a busy day?

91
00:03:51,466 --> 00:03:52,333
Yes.

92
00:03:52,399 --> 00:03:54,433
I've been working very hard.

93
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:57,799
We've been working very hard, too.

94
00:03:58,033 --> 00:04:00,700
We've been shopkeepers.

95
00:04:03,299 --> 00:04:06,799
Blah, blah, blah, the end.

96
00:04:07,033 --> 00:04:08,100
And print.

97
00:04:09,366 --> 00:04:11,666
[narrator] Mommy Pig
has finished her work.

98
00:04:11,733 --> 00:04:13,200
[George giggles, then snorts]

99
00:04:13,266 --> 00:04:18,066
Okay, George, perhaps we can just play
one game of Happy Mrs. Chicken.

100
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:19,166
We've earned it.

101
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:21,700
[squawks, then farting]

102
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:24,800
[George giggling]

103
00:04:25,766 --> 00:04:27,300
Naughty, Mommy.

104
00:04:27,366 --> 00:04:30,166
You're playing Happy Mrs. Chicken.

105
00:04:30,233 --> 00:04:33,500
Oh, that's because George and I
have finished our work.

106
00:04:33,566 --> 00:04:35,333
-Haven't we, George?
-[snorts]

107
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:39,366
We've all finished our work,
so, let's all play.

108
00:04:40,099 --> 00:04:42,099
[chickens farting]

109
00:04:43,166 --> 00:04:45,166
[all laughing]

110
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:49,666
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

111
00:04:49,733 --> 00:04:53,200
[narrator] Peppa and her family are going
for a drive to the mountains.

112
00:04:53,266 --> 00:04:56,166
[snorts] Are we nearly there yet?

113
00:04:56,233 --> 00:04:57,800
[snorts] Not yet, Peppa.

114
00:04:58,033 --> 00:04:58,800
[both sigh]

115
00:04:59,033 --> 00:05:00,466
Let's play a game.

116
00:05:00,533 --> 00:05:03,633
We each have to spot a car
of our favorite color.

117
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:05,000
[Peppa &amp; George] Yes!

118
00:05:05,066 --> 00:05:07,400
My favorite color is green.

119
00:05:07,733 --> 00:05:09,633
Mine is orange.

120
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,666
[snorts] Mine is red.

121
00:05:11,733 --> 00:05:14,566
George, what's your favorite color?

122
00:05:14,633 --> 00:05:15,500
Boo.

123
00:05:15,566 --> 00:05:17,599
[narrator] George's favorite color
is blue.

124
00:05:18,233 --> 00:05:21,233
[snorts] Let's see which color car
comes along first.

125
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:22,533
[children &amp; Mommy Pig] Okay.

126
00:05:22,599 --> 00:05:23,466
[horn honks]

127
00:05:23,533 --> 00:05:26,133
[narrator] Here is Candy Cat
in her green car.

128
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:29,633
[chuckles] Green.
That's my favorite color.

129
00:05:30,266 --> 00:05:31,333
I win.

130
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:33,266
[snorts] Hello, Candy.

131
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:35,166
[meows] Hello, Peppa.

132
00:05:36,233 --> 00:05:37,133
[horn honks]

133
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:40,300
[narrator] Here is Danny Dog
in Granddad Dog's breakdown truck.

134
00:05:40,366 --> 00:05:42,233
[snorts] Orange. So, I win.

135
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,800
Hello, Danny.

136
00:05:44,033 --> 00:05:45,566
[woofs] Hello, Peppa.

137
00:05:45,633 --> 00:05:48,166
[laughs] Here's another car.

138
00:05:48,233 --> 00:05:50,766
-[horn honks]
-[Peppa] It's Suzy. Hello.

139
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,700
[bleats] Hello, Peppa.

140
00:05:52,766 --> 00:05:55,166
-[snorts] Boo.
-Yes, George.

141
00:05:55,233 --> 00:05:57,800
It's a blue car, so, you win.

142
00:05:58,033 --> 00:05:59,666
[giggles]

143
00:05:59,733 --> 00:06:02,466
[sighs] This is a silly game.

144
00:06:02,533 --> 00:06:05,500
There isn't a red car anywhere.

145
00:06:05,566 --> 00:06:08,400
There is one red car, Peppa.

146
00:06:08,466 --> 00:06:09,400
Where?

147
00:06:09,466 --> 00:06:11,133
[Daddy Pig laughs]

148
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:13,800
What color is our car?

149
00:06:14,033 --> 00:06:16,266
Uh... it's red.

150
00:06:16,333 --> 00:06:18,000
I win! I win!

151
00:06:18,066 --> 00:06:19,766
[all laughing]

152
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:23,366
[narrator] The family have arrived
at the mountains.

153
00:06:23,433 --> 00:06:27,000
We'll have a fantastic view
when we get to the top.

154
00:06:28,299 --> 00:06:29,299
We're here.

155
00:06:29,366 --> 00:06:30,633
[all] Hooray!

156
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:33,633
Look at the lovely sunny view.

157
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:34,766
[all yell]

158
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,133
[narrator] Oh, dear.
It has started to rain.

159
00:06:37,566 --> 00:06:40,366
Where's the lovely view?

160
00:06:40,433 --> 00:06:43,033
Uh... there's a lovely view.

161
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:45,733
[narrator] It is Miss Rabbit's
ice-cream stall.

162
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:47,366
Hello, Miss Rabbit.

163
00:06:47,433 --> 00:06:49,099
Hello, Daddy Pig.

164
00:06:49,166 --> 00:06:51,066
Four ice creams, please.

165
00:06:51,133 --> 00:06:52,733
What flavors would you like?

166
00:06:52,799 --> 00:06:57,233
Mint, orange, strawberry
and blueberry, please.

167
00:06:57,700 --> 00:06:58,566
Okay.

168
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:01,700
[chuckles]

169
00:07:01,766 --> 00:07:03,466
Look what I've got.

170
00:07:03,533 --> 00:07:05,099
-Ice cream!
-[George snorts]

171
00:07:05,166 --> 00:07:06,299
Oh. [chuckles]

172
00:07:06,366 --> 00:07:08,533
They're our favorite colors.

173
00:07:08,599 --> 00:07:10,133
That's right. [snorts]

174
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,433
Green for me.

175
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:12,700
Orange for me.

176
00:07:13,299 --> 00:07:15,366
Strawberry red for me.

177
00:07:15,799 --> 00:07:17,099
And George's is...

178
00:07:17,166 --> 00:07:18,400
Boo.

179
00:07:18,466 --> 00:07:20,366
[George giggles]

180
00:07:20,433 --> 00:07:21,299
Yum, yum, yum.

181
00:07:21,366 --> 00:07:23,000
-Yummy.
-Look.

182
00:07:23,066 --> 00:07:25,200
The sun has come out.

183
00:07:25,266 --> 00:07:27,266
[Daddy Pig] And look what else
has come out.

184
00:07:27,333 --> 00:07:29,133
[George &amp; Peppa] A rainbow!

185
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:31,766
[narrator] Peppa and George love rainbows.

186
00:07:32,266 --> 00:07:34,233
[Daddy Pig] A rainbow only comes out

187
00:07:34,299 --> 00:07:37,533
when it's rainy and sunny
at the same time.

188
00:07:38,133 --> 00:07:39,200
[both] Ooh.

189
00:07:39,266 --> 00:07:42,500
It's got all our favorite colors in it.

190
00:07:42,566 --> 00:07:44,200
[Peppa] Yes. [snorts]

191
00:07:44,266 --> 00:07:47,666
Red and orange and green and blue.

192
00:07:47,733 --> 00:07:49,666
[both giggling]

193
00:07:49,733 --> 00:07:54,000
And do you know what you find
at the end of a rainbow?

194
00:07:54,066 --> 00:07:55,233
[both] No.

195
00:07:55,299 --> 00:07:56,799
You find treasure.

196
00:07:57,033 --> 00:08:01,233
Oh! Can we go and find the treasure now?

197
00:08:01,299 --> 00:08:02,400
Okay.

198
00:08:02,466 --> 00:08:06,200
The end of the rainbow looks like
it's just on the next hill.

199
00:08:06,266 --> 00:08:07,500
Let's go.

200
00:08:08,366 --> 00:08:10,733
[all] Whee!

201
00:08:10,799 --> 00:08:12,133
[Daddy Pig &amp; Peppa giggle]

202
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:14,566
♪ It's a rainy sunny day ♪

203
00:08:14,633 --> 00:08:17,033
The rainbow's here to play ♪

204
00:08:17,099 --> 00:08:19,533
♪ Rainbow, rainbow ♪

205
00:08:19,599 --> 00:08:24,666
♪ Red and orange and yellow and green
And purple and blue ♪

206
00:08:24,733 --> 00:08:27,000
♪ Rainbow, rainbow ♪

207
00:08:27,066 --> 00:08:29,766
♪ It's a rainy sunny day ♪

208
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,099
[Peppa &amp; George giggle]

209
00:08:31,166 --> 00:08:32,233
Here we are.

210
00:08:32,666 --> 00:08:35,466
Oh. Where's our rainbow gone?

211
00:08:35,533 --> 00:08:37,533
It's moved to the next hill.

212
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,400
You cheeky rainbow.

213
00:08:39,466 --> 00:08:41,199
Quick, let's catch it.

214
00:08:41,633 --> 00:08:44,166
♪ Rainbow, rainbow ♪

215
00:08:44,233 --> 00:08:46,199
♪ It's a rainy sunny day ♪

216
00:08:46,699 --> 00:08:48,300
It's stopped raining.

217
00:08:49,566 --> 00:08:51,566
And the rainbow is gone.

218
00:08:52,166 --> 00:08:55,066
-[George crying]
-[Mommy Pig] Don't worry, George.

219
00:08:55,533 --> 00:08:58,699
Maybe the rainbow has left
some treasure behind.

220
00:08:58,766 --> 00:09:00,533
There's something over here.

221
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:03,199
Have you found the rainbow's treasure?

222
00:09:03,266 --> 00:09:05,699
Yes, I have.

223
00:09:05,766 --> 00:09:08,533
A big, muddy puddle.

224
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:10,000
[all] Hooray!

225
00:09:10,066 --> 00:09:11,600
[all laughing]

226
00:09:11,666 --> 00:09:15,000
This is the best rainbow treasure ever.

227
00:09:15,066 --> 00:09:16,766
[all laughing]

228
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:22,266
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

229
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:23,666
[narrator] It is a school day.

230
00:09:24,166 --> 00:09:26,566
Peppa and her friends
are having a music lesson.

231
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:29,300
♪ Oh ♪

232
00:09:29,366 --> 00:09:31,600
♪ Miss Polly had a dolly ♪

233
00:09:31,666 --> 00:09:32,633
[Pedro coughing]

234
00:09:32,699 --> 00:09:35,366
Sorry, Madame Gazelle. [coughs]

235
00:09:35,433 --> 00:09:37,566
[narrator] Oh, dear. Pedro has a cough.

236
00:09:37,633 --> 00:09:39,100
Not to worry.

237
00:09:39,166 --> 00:09:41,666
I'll ring Dr. Brown Bear.

238
00:09:41,733 --> 00:09:43,466
[dialing]

239
00:09:43,533 --> 00:09:45,033
[ringing]

240
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:46,666
Dr. Brown Bear speaking.

241
00:09:46,733 --> 00:09:49,199
Hello, doctor, this is Madame Gazelle.

242
00:09:49,666 --> 00:09:51,066
A child is ill.

243
00:09:51,133 --> 00:09:52,533
Don't panic.

244
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:54,333
I'll come straightaway.

245
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:59,033
[siren wailing]

246
00:10:02,366 --> 00:10:04,100
[Dr. Brown Bear panting]

247
00:10:04,166 --> 00:10:08,300
-What seems to be the problem?
-I've got a cough. [coughs]

248
00:10:08,366 --> 00:10:09,500
I see.

249
00:10:09,566 --> 00:10:13,199
Is it a tickly cough or a chesty cough?

250
00:10:13,266 --> 00:10:15,500
Um... I don't know.

251
00:10:15,566 --> 00:10:18,000
But it goes like this:

252
00:10:18,066 --> 00:10:19,433
-[Pedro coughs]
-Hmm.

253
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:22,066
And when did you get this cough?

254
00:10:22,133 --> 00:10:25,300
When Madame Gazelle started singing.

255
00:10:25,366 --> 00:10:30,433
It's nothing serious,
but Pedro's cough may be catching.

256
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:33,266
What do you mean, "catching"?

257
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:35,366
When one person has a cough,

258
00:10:35,433 --> 00:10:38,233
sometimes, other people
get that cough, too.

259
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:40,066
Do I need medicine?

260
00:10:40,133 --> 00:10:42,433
Just a little spoonful.

261
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:45,300
I'm afraid it doesn't taste very nice.

262
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:47,066
Ugh!

263
00:10:47,133 --> 00:10:50,566
It tastes like an old shoe full of jam.

264
00:10:50,633 --> 00:10:53,133
Thank you, Dr. Brown Bear.

265
00:10:53,199 --> 00:10:55,400
-Goodbye.
-[students] Bye.

266
00:10:55,466 --> 00:10:57,133
[both cough]

267
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:58,800
As I thought.

268
00:10:59,033 --> 00:11:01,666
Pedro's cough is catching.

269
00:11:02,633 --> 00:11:05,300
[narrator] Danny Dog and Suzy Sheep
have caught Pedro's cough.

270
00:11:05,366 --> 00:11:06,733
[Suzy &amp; Danny cough]

271
00:11:07,366 --> 00:11:08,266
Open wide.

272
00:11:09,233 --> 00:11:10,266
Ew!

273
00:11:10,333 --> 00:11:14,466
It tastes of carpet-flavored yogurt.

274
00:11:14,533 --> 00:11:15,699
Ugh!

275
00:11:15,766 --> 00:11:18,333
It tastes of flowers.

276
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:21,600
Well done for taking your medicine
so well.

277
00:11:21,666 --> 00:11:25,266
Do you ever get ill, Dr. Brown Bear?

278
00:11:25,333 --> 00:11:27,166
No, Peppa, I'm never ill.

279
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,600
I eat an apple a day.

280
00:11:31,533 --> 00:11:33,433
-Goodbye.
-[students] Bye.

281
00:11:34,033 --> 00:11:35,100
[ringing]

282
00:11:35,166 --> 00:11:36,400
[narrator] It is home time.

283
00:11:36,466 --> 00:11:39,100
The children's parents are here
to pick them up.

284
00:11:39,166 --> 00:11:43,533
Mommy, Daddy, I've got a cough. [coughs]

285
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:47,199
Dr. Brown Bear came
and looked after us.

286
00:11:47,266 --> 00:11:50,400
He gave us horrible medicine.

287
00:11:50,466 --> 00:11:53,800
Madame Gazelle, can you sing
your song now?

288
00:11:54,033 --> 00:11:55,333
Of course, Peppa.

289
00:11:56,199 --> 00:11:58,033
♪ Oh ♪

290
00:11:58,100 --> 00:12:01,133
♪ Miss Polly had a dolly who was ♪

291
00:12:01,199 --> 00:12:03,199
[coughs]

292
00:12:03,266 --> 00:12:05,266
[all coughing]

293
00:12:06,633 --> 00:12:10,300
[narrator] Oh, dear. All the grown-ups
have caught Pedro's cough.

294
00:12:10,366 --> 00:12:12,300
[rings]

295
00:12:12,366 --> 00:12:14,300
Dr. Brown Bear speaking.

296
00:12:14,366 --> 00:12:16,266
This is Peppa Pig. [snorts]

297
00:12:16,333 --> 00:12:18,366
All the grown-ups are ill.

298
00:12:18,433 --> 00:12:19,733
Not to worry. Peppa.

299
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:21,133
I'm on my way.

300
00:12:21,733 --> 00:12:23,733
[siren wailing]

301
00:12:25,633 --> 00:12:27,500
[grown-ups coughing]

302
00:12:28,166 --> 00:12:29,500
Hello, everyone.

303
00:12:29,566 --> 00:12:31,566
Caught Pedro's cough, have we?

304
00:12:31,633 --> 00:12:33,566
[all coughing]

305
00:12:33,633 --> 00:12:34,566
Very well,

306
00:12:34,633 --> 00:12:38,000
stand in line and open wide.

307
00:12:38,599 --> 00:12:43,033
[all] Ew.

308
00:12:43,099 --> 00:12:46,266
It tastes like custard and old socks.

309
00:12:46,333 --> 00:12:47,500
[all laugh]

310
00:12:47,566 --> 00:12:50,666
Thank you for looking after us,
Dr. Brown Bear.

311
00:12:50,733 --> 00:12:53,633
Who looks after you when you're ill?

312
00:12:53,699 --> 00:12:55,500
No one looks after me.

313
00:12:55,566 --> 00:12:56,766
I'm never ill.

314
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,266
[coughing]

315
00:12:59,333 --> 00:13:02,433
[narrator] Oh, dear.
Dr. Brown Bear has caught Pedro's cough.

316
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:04,333
Not to worry. [coughs]

317
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:05,466
Goodbye.

318
00:13:05,533 --> 00:13:06,766
[all] Goodbye.

319
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
Poor Dr. Brown Bear.

320
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:12,733
He's ill and there's no one
to look after him.

321
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:14,233
[all] Oh.

322
00:13:15,666 --> 00:13:17,800
[coughing]

323
00:13:21,233 --> 00:13:22,099
[doorbell rings]

324
00:13:22,166 --> 00:13:23,266
Who can that be?

325
00:13:23,733 --> 00:13:24,666
Hello.

326
00:13:24,733 --> 00:13:27,000
We've come to look after you.

327
00:13:27,066 --> 00:13:28,699
[woofs] Here's some fruit.

328
00:13:28,766 --> 00:13:31,500
[neighs] And some cushions.

329
00:13:31,566 --> 00:13:33,699
And here is your medicine.

330
00:13:33,766 --> 00:13:35,033
Ew.

331
00:13:35,099 --> 00:13:39,766
It tastes like jammy yogurt-flavored
custard socks.

332
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,400
[children giggle]

333
00:13:41,466 --> 00:13:45,099
And here's a song to make you feel better.

334
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,633
♪ Oh ♪

335
00:13:50,066 --> 00:13:51,633
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

336
00:13:51,699 --> 00:13:53,233
[narrator] It is bedtime.

337
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:54,566
Good night, Peppa.

338
00:13:54,633 --> 00:13:56,099
Good night, George.

339
00:13:56,166 --> 00:13:59,333
[snorts] Can I have a story, please?

340
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:00,300
Okay.

341
00:14:00,366 --> 00:14:02,733
I'll read you The Red Monkey book.

342
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:05,300
But we always have that one.

343
00:14:05,366 --> 00:14:10,166
The Red Monkey has a bath,
cleans his teeth, and goes to sleep.

344
00:14:10,233 --> 00:14:13,533
Uh... Yes, that is what happens.

345
00:14:13,599 --> 00:14:16,433
Can we choose another story?

346
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:21,533
The Blue Tiger, The Green Spider,
The Orange Penguin.

347
00:14:21,599 --> 00:14:24,133
Oh! What's this one?

348
00:14:24,199 --> 00:14:26,666
The Wonderful World of Concrete.

349
00:14:26,733 --> 00:14:28,666
I've been looking for that.

350
00:14:28,733 --> 00:14:31,066
Is it your book, Daddy?

351
00:14:31,133 --> 00:14:33,699
It's a book I borrowed from the library.

352
00:14:33,766 --> 00:14:36,133
What's a library?

353
00:14:36,199 --> 00:14:38,599
It's a place you borrow books from.

354
00:14:38,666 --> 00:14:42,233
When you've finished reading them,
you take them back.

355
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:45,333
But Daddy Pig has forgotten
to take this book back.

356
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:48,466
I have had it for rather a long time.

357
00:14:48,533 --> 00:14:51,533
Never mind.
You can take it back tomorrow. [snorts]

358
00:14:51,599 --> 00:14:53,533
But now it's bedtime.

359
00:14:53,599 --> 00:14:56,366
After Daddy reads this story.

360
00:14:56,433 --> 00:14:58,599
It's not much of a story, Peppa.

361
00:14:58,666 --> 00:15:00,699
Please read it, Daddy.

362
00:15:00,766 --> 00:15:02,166
Okay.

363
00:15:02,233 --> 00:15:03,666
[giggles]

364
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:06,533
The Wonderful World of Concrete.

365
00:15:07,133 --> 00:15:09,533
"Concrete is a construction material

366
00:15:09,599 --> 00:15:14,033
composed of sand, water
and chemical admixtures.

367
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,566
Chapter one, sand."

368
00:15:16,633 --> 00:15:19,000
[Mommy Pig &amp; children snoring]

369
00:15:19,066 --> 00:15:22,366
[narrator] Peppa, George and Mommy Pig
have fallen asleep.

370
00:15:24,766 --> 00:15:25,733
It is morning.

371
00:15:26,266 --> 00:15:28,733
Peppa and her family have come
to the library.

372
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,500
[Peppa &amp; George giggling]

373
00:15:30,566 --> 00:15:34,366
-Wow! What a lot of books.
-Shh.

374
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:37,666
Peppa, you must be quiet in the library.

375
00:15:37,733 --> 00:15:39,000
Why?

376
00:15:39,066 --> 00:15:43,566
Because people come here to read
and to be quiet.

377
00:15:43,633 --> 00:15:45,366
Next, please.

378
00:15:45,433 --> 00:15:47,566
[narrator] Miss Rabbit is the librarian.

379
00:15:47,633 --> 00:15:50,699
Hello, Mommy Pig.
Are you returning these books?

380
00:15:50,766 --> 00:15:53,099
-Yes, Miss Rabbit.
-Right you are.

381
00:15:53,566 --> 00:15:55,666
[computer beeping]

382
00:15:55,733 --> 00:15:59,166
-Why is the computer beeping?
-It's checking to see

383
00:15:59,233 --> 00:16:02,566
that you haven't been naughty
and borrowed the book for too long.

384
00:16:02,633 --> 00:16:06,333
Um... I may have borrowed this book
for a bit too long.

385
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:09,000
Oh. Don't worry, Daddy Pig.

386
00:16:09,066 --> 00:16:10,400
It can't be that bad.

387
00:16:11,066 --> 00:16:12,599
[blaring]

388
00:16:12,666 --> 00:16:18,099
Gosh, Daddy Pig, you've had this book out
for ten years.

389
00:16:18,166 --> 00:16:19,599
Naughty, Daddy.

390
00:16:19,666 --> 00:16:21,166
Sorry, Miss Rabbit.

391
00:16:21,233 --> 00:16:22,400
That's all right.

392
00:16:22,466 --> 00:16:24,433
Now you can borrow another book.

393
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:29,333
Miss Rabbit, can George and I
borrow a book, please?

394
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:30,366
Yes.

395
00:16:30,433 --> 00:16:33,199
The children's section is over here.

396
00:16:33,266 --> 00:16:34,633
[Peppa &amp; George giggle]

397
00:16:34,699 --> 00:16:35,699
Oh, look.

398
00:16:35,766 --> 00:16:40,066
Fairies, flowers, pretty dresses.

399
00:16:40,133 --> 00:16:41,666
[woofs] Hello, Peppa.

400
00:16:41,733 --> 00:16:43,533
Oh, hello, Danny.

401
00:16:43,599 --> 00:16:46,300
I'm borrowing a book about football.

402
00:16:46,366 --> 00:16:49,099
[bleats] Hello, Peppa.

403
00:16:49,166 --> 00:16:50,366
[snorts] Hello, Suzy.

404
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:54,033
-I've got a book about nurses.
-[George snorts]

405
00:16:54,099 --> 00:16:57,066
[narrator] George has chosen a book
about dinosaurs.

406
00:16:57,133 --> 00:16:59,466
Dine-saw. Grr.

407
00:16:59,533 --> 00:17:01,766
[snorts] Look what I've found.

408
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,800
Further Adventures
in the World of Concrete.

409
00:17:06,399 --> 00:17:08,166
Here's a Red Monkey book.

410
00:17:08,233 --> 00:17:10,566
Not the Red Monkey book.

411
00:17:10,633 --> 00:17:12,566
It's boring.

412
00:17:12,633 --> 00:17:14,733
But this is a different story.

413
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:16,466
It might be more fun.

414
00:17:16,533 --> 00:17:18,266
I bet it's not.

415
00:17:19,066 --> 00:17:22,366
"Once upon a time,
there was a Red Monkey..."

416
00:17:22,433 --> 00:17:27,200
Ugh. He had a bath, cleaned his teeth
and went to bed.

417
00:17:27,266 --> 00:17:28,133
[Mommy Pig] No.

418
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:31,399
"He jumped in a space rocket
and went to the moon.

419
00:17:31,466 --> 00:17:32,633
[children] Ooh.

420
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:36,399
[Mommy Pig] He had a picnic
with a dinosaur and swam under the sea

421
00:17:36,466 --> 00:17:39,033
and climbed the highest mountain.

422
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:40,333
That was a busy day.

423
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:41,700
The end."

424
00:17:41,766 --> 00:17:44,066
Wow! Read it again.

425
00:17:44,133 --> 00:17:47,066
We can borrow it
and read it at home, Peppa.

426
00:17:47,133 --> 00:17:52,466
But I was going to choose this book
or this one.

427
00:17:52,533 --> 00:17:55,500
You can take three books home
if you want, Peppa.

428
00:17:55,566 --> 00:17:56,666
Yippee!

429
00:17:56,733 --> 00:18:00,066
But you must remember
to bring them back on time.

430
00:18:00,133 --> 00:18:01,700
Yes, Miss Rabbit.

431
00:18:01,766 --> 00:18:07,300
And you must remember
to bring your book back, too, Daddy Pig.

432
00:18:07,366 --> 00:18:10,633
[giggles] I'll make sure Daddy remembers.

433
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:14,033
Yes, Peppa, I'm sure you will.

434
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:16,100
[all laughing]

435
00:18:21,133 --> 00:18:23,266
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

436
00:18:23,333 --> 00:18:26,366
[narrator] Peppa and George
are very excited today.

437
00:18:26,433 --> 00:18:28,266
They are going on holiday.

438
00:18:28,333 --> 00:18:30,200
Oh, where's Daddy?

439
00:18:30,266 --> 00:18:33,399
[snorts] He's bringing a secret surprise.

440
00:18:33,466 --> 00:18:34,600
[horn honking]

441
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:36,800
What's that?

442
00:18:37,033 --> 00:18:39,166
[snorts] It's a camper van.

443
00:18:39,233 --> 00:18:41,666
We've borrowed it for our holiday.

444
00:18:41,733 --> 00:18:43,300
Ooh.

445
00:18:43,366 --> 00:18:45,500
This camper van has everything.

446
00:18:46,133 --> 00:18:47,666
This button works the sink.

447
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,333
[both] Wow.

448
00:18:50,399 --> 00:18:53,033
And this button works the TV.

449
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:54,566
[both giggling]

450
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,733
What does this button do?

451
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:57,733
I'm not sure.

452
00:18:58,466 --> 00:19:01,166
Maybe don't press it until we know.

453
00:19:01,233 --> 00:19:03,633
[snorts] Is everybody ready
to go on holiday?

454
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:05,600
[Daddy Pig &amp; children] Yes, Mommy Pig.

455
00:19:05,666 --> 00:19:08,066
Then let's go.

456
00:19:09,166 --> 00:19:10,033
[Peppa giggles]

457
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:13,300
♪ We're going on holiday
In a camper van ♪

458
00:19:13,366 --> 00:19:14,333
[horn honks]

459
00:19:14,399 --> 00:19:15,800
[all laugh]

460
00:19:16,033 --> 00:19:18,500
Hmm. This map is a bit tricky.

461
00:19:19,100 --> 00:19:22,366
Daddy, we don't want to get lost.

462
00:19:22,433 --> 00:19:23,800
[Daddy Pig] Don't worry, Peppa.

463
00:19:24,033 --> 00:19:26,166
I'm an expert at map reading.

464
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,200
Oh, that's strange.

465
00:19:29,266 --> 00:19:31,533
-Are we lost?
-Uh...

466
00:19:32,133 --> 00:19:33,133
Yes.

467
00:19:34,666 --> 00:19:37,300
[narrator] It's Granddad Dog
with Danny Dog.

468
00:19:37,366 --> 00:19:39,233
[woofs] Hello, Peppa.

469
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,633
Hello, Danny.

470
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:42,133
We're lost.

471
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:44,266
[woofs] Lost?

472
00:19:44,333 --> 00:19:46,033
Is your satnav broken?

473
00:19:46,100 --> 00:19:47,566
Satnav?

474
00:19:47,633 --> 00:19:51,700
You're driving a camper van T3200.

475
00:19:51,766 --> 00:19:53,766
Satnav comes as standard.

476
00:19:54,666 --> 00:19:57,133
[computer] Welcome to the car
of the future.

477
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,766
Ah.

478
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,600
So, that's what that button does.

479
00:20:01,666 --> 00:20:03,766
[computer] Where are we going today?

480
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,700
The camper van is talking.

481
00:20:06,766 --> 00:20:08,166
Clever, isn't it?

482
00:20:08,466 --> 00:20:11,433
The computer voice helps you
find your way.

483
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:15,133
But how does it know where we want to go?

484
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:16,233
You tell it.

485
00:20:16,666 --> 00:20:20,233
Uh, hello, Mrs. Camper Van.

486
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:21,533
[computer] Hello.

487
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:25,366
We're going on holiday.
Can you tell us the way?

488
00:20:25,433 --> 00:20:29,433
[computer] Proceed on the current road
in a straight line.

489
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:31,700
Thanks for your help, Granddad Dog.

490
00:20:31,766 --> 00:20:33,066
You're welcome.

491
00:20:33,133 --> 00:20:34,399
Have a lovely holiday.

492
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:39,033
♪ We're going on holiday
In a camper van ♪

493
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:40,333
[all laughing]

494
00:20:40,399 --> 00:20:41,433
[alarm blaring]

495
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:43,399
[computer] Danger, danger.

496
00:20:43,466 --> 00:20:45,100
Oil is low.

497
00:20:45,566 --> 00:20:47,000
What's oil?

498
00:20:47,066 --> 00:20:50,433
Oil helps engines to run smoothly.

499
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:53,066
Will the oil run out?

500
00:20:53,133 --> 00:20:54,266
No.

501
00:20:54,333 --> 00:20:57,266
These warnings always give you
plenty of time.

502
00:20:57,733 --> 00:20:59,500
[computer] Oil is gone.

503
00:20:59,566 --> 00:21:00,800
[engine clunks]

504
00:21:01,033 --> 00:21:02,500
Oh, dear.

505
00:21:02,566 --> 00:21:06,100
Luckily, I've got a spare can of oil.

506
00:21:06,166 --> 00:21:07,733
Well done, Daddy Pig.

507
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:12,166
[snorts] We simply pour the oil
into the engine and--

508
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:13,766
-Oh.
-What's wrong?

509
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:15,800
There's nothing in here.

510
00:21:16,033 --> 00:21:18,100
The engine's gone.

511
00:21:18,166 --> 00:21:19,333
[horn honks]

512
00:21:19,399 --> 00:21:22,033
[narrator] It's Mommy Sheep
with Suzy Sheep.

513
00:21:22,466 --> 00:21:23,733
Hello, Suzy.

514
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:25,666
[bleats] Hello, Peppa.

515
00:21:25,733 --> 00:21:28,166
We've lost our engine.

516
00:21:28,633 --> 00:21:30,333
Lost your engine?

517
00:21:30,399 --> 00:21:33,433
Yes. [snorts] It's completely disappeared.

518
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:34,733
I'd like to help,

519
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:37,466
but I don't know a thing about engines.

520
00:21:38,266 --> 00:21:43,100
I'm probably just being silly,
but this looks a bit like an engine.

521
00:21:43,166 --> 00:21:44,433
Oh, yes.

522
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:46,633
Well spotted, Mommy Sheep.

523
00:21:46,700 --> 00:21:49,766
[narrator] The camper van has its engine
at the back.

524
00:21:51,766 --> 00:21:52,633
There.

525
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:55,366
That should be enough oil.

526
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:57,333
Thank you, Mommy Sheep.

527
00:21:57,399 --> 00:21:58,633
You're welcome.

528
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:00,466
Have a lovely holiday.

529
00:22:02,700 --> 00:22:04,733
Are we nearly there yet?

530
00:22:05,266 --> 00:22:07,433
[computer] Just up the next hill.

531
00:22:08,433 --> 00:22:11,066
You have reached your destination.

532
00:22:11,133 --> 00:22:12,533
[all] Hooray!

533
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:13,766
Time for bed.

534
00:22:15,466 --> 00:22:17,733
[snorts] Where will we sleep?

535
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:21,666
Mommy Pig and I will sleep on this bed.

536
00:22:21,733 --> 00:22:23,000
Ooh.

537
00:22:23,066 --> 00:22:27,633
-And you two will sleep upstairs.
-But there isn't an upstairs.

538
00:22:27,700 --> 00:22:30,333
Oh-ho. Watch this.

539
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:34,399
[narrator] The camper van's roof
is lifting up.

540
00:22:35,333 --> 00:22:39,766
[Peppa] The camper van is just like
our little house. [giggles]

541
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:43,200
While we're on holiday,
it is our little house.

542
00:22:43,266 --> 00:22:44,633
[Peppa &amp; George giggle]

543
00:22:44,700 --> 00:22:47,000
[Daddy Pig] Good night, my little piggies.

544
00:22:47,066 --> 00:22:48,166
[Peppa] Good night.

545
00:22:50,600 --> 00:22:52,133
-[child giggles]
-[Peppa snorts]

546
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:53,466
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

547
00:22:53,533 --> 00:22:55,600
-[Peppa snorts]
-[child giggles]

548
00:22:55,666 --> 00:22:56,533
[Peppa snorts]

549
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:58,266
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

550
00:22:58,333 --> 00:23:00,666
-[Peppa snorts]
-[children giggle]

551
00:23:00,733 --> 00:23:02,333
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

552
00:23:02,399 --> 00:23:04,033
-[Peppa snorts]
-[children giggle]

